A||||21||RobertVol||Need opinions, White or Burgundy?||||5||
Z||000000||RobertVol||04-08-2001||05:07 PM||||Well some $*@&$(@ Idiot backed into the rear of my GT and thank goodness all he did was scratch the tail end up and bend the tailpipes. Could have been worse I guess. <P>Anyway here is the question <P>I was thinking of painting my car another color, If you look in my signature its a 88 GT white non spoiler T top. The car only has 60K miles on it. Now I know the purists would say keep it stock but I would love to paint it Burgundy. of course the GM color code for the fiero would be used. Now it would still be sorta of stock. <P>Being that My car is a Wing Delete optioned car I have never seen a a wing delete 88 GT with T tops, in that color.I have seen them with the wing though and I think I would like it without it. Whats everyones take?<P>Maybe I can get one of you great picture altering gurus to give what one would look like. <P>Thanks as always. <P>PS. Is anybody else realize what a great forum we have? I love it !  <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierofreek2001||04-08-2001||05:33 PM||||hey man, sorry to hear about your car, but i think you should keep the white! its soo soo beautiful, white/tan/t-tops!! AHHHHH  plus if you paint it the same color, you wont notice if the painter missed a spot, or didnt cut in the doors or whatever.... white all the way!<BR>steve<BR>WHITE 85 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||04-08-2001||07:02 PM||||I vote to keep it white.  White/Tan/Gold rims go together very well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||04-08-2001||07:06 PM||||hmmm well thats 2 whites and no burgundy votes.. well I may leave it white then but I love that other color.<P>I may have to break down and buy another one <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||04-08-2001||08:21 PM||||Any color will look great if it's well kept.  However, darker colors really show the dust and nicks, plus they really get HOT in the summer sun.  I say keep it white and keep it clean!||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||04-08-2001||08:36 PM||||*Please* keep it white - *especially* with the tan interior. I've *always* wanted a white GT without the wing - reminds me of the Testarossa on Miami Vice...||||reg||1
Z||000006||ArchMagi||04-08-2001||09:25 PM||||I vote burgundy! thats my colour  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>and btw, does anyone know the colour code for burgundy? ||||reg||1
