Z||000009||RobertVol||04-08-2001||11:28 PM||||Duh! Lar! <P>I should have looked at that picture!<BR>I have posted on our site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Thakns for posting again. It really gives an option. I love the monochromatic 88 GT in Burgundy and like it with gold rims but White does not show that much like was said. hmmmm.... DECISIONS DECISIONS.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 04-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||banditbalz||04-08-2001||11:35 PM||||My vote is for white. It just shows better with the contrasting colour of the black tires, trim, windows, etc. Plus, you don't ever have to worry about overspray/underspray.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||2
Z||000011||Oreif||04-09-2001||12:26 AM||||Well I like white Fiero's and I like the Burgundy ones too! But I would have to say that my choice would be to keep it white.<BR>I am not too sure how the tan interior would look on the burgundy car. Does any one have a burgundy with tan?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Songman||04-09-2001||12:55 AM||||Hey Robert,<P>I think your car looks great just the way it is.... And besides, if you paint it burgundy it will be too much like this one I am getting...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/tnfieros/88t-top.jpg">   <P>Of course, this one will be white when I am done with it! With Indy stylings of course...<P>I'll be in Jacksonville Thursday through Sunday... wanna try again to get together?<P>dang! that picture was huge! Hope this is better...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Kelvin Vivian||04-09-2001||02:05 AM||||My vote would be for you to keep it white. A white 88 GT looks sharp. Plus it'll remain stock, I've not seen too many white 88 GT T-tops... Seen lots of bright red ones.<P>Oreif, I know that in 88 some of the burgundy cars came with a tan interior...<P>There was a very sharp, original, 88 GT T-top that was 4-sale on eBay about 2 months ago. Did anyone else see it, or know of the car I'm talking about? It was a stock medium red metallic, low mileage ~16k or so, 5-spd, beechwood interior, leather seats, gold wheels, and I believe it sold for $16,000.  <P>I "watched" the eBay sale in "My eBay" lemme go see if the page still exists...<P>Nope, the page no longer exists... Wish I had saved the pics, it was the sharpest original 88 GT T-top I've seen, gold wheels and tan interior to boot! Made me second guess whether or not I liked mine "bright red" (but only for a minute  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)... If you do decide to go 88 burgundy, you won't be disappointed...<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high">    <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||10:13 AM||||Well... I just advised another Forum member to paint his car the color that made him happy. The same advise goes to you. Personally, I like just about any color BUT burgundy. It is the MOST produced of all colors in the Fiero model. Just take a look at the production numbers. Too common!<P>Something to consider... if your going to change colors, look at ALL colors for ALL makes of cars. There are some really nice colors out there just waiting to grace to skin of a really clean Fiero.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
